---
import Head from '../components/Head.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/global.css';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <Head
      title="About"
      description="What news.dehor.com.br is, who publishes it, and which open-source projects it covers."
      canonicalURL={new URL('/about', Astro.site)}
    />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
  </head>
  <body>
    <Nav />

    <main>
      <section class="section" aria-labelledby="about-title">
        <div class="container container--narrow">
          <article class="prose">
            <h1 id="about-title">About news.dehor.com.br</h1>
            <p>
              news.dehor.com.br is the publication and project log of Nikolas de Hor, a developer based in Goiânia, GO, Brazil. It is a personal, non-commercial site built with <a href="https://astro.build" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Astro</a> and deployed on Vercel.
            </p>
            <h2>What it publishes</h2>
            <p>
              Each entry ("edição") is a dated update about one of the open-source projects
              maintained under the DeHor Labs organization. There is no editorial staff and no
              paid content; every post is written by Nikolas de Hor about his own work.
            </p>
            <h2>Projects covered</h2>
            <ul>
              <li>
                <a href="/mcp-fiscal-brasil/">MCP Fiscal Brasil</a> - an open-source MCP (Model Context Protocol) server for Brazilian fiscal data, published on <a href="https://github.com/DeHor-Labs/mcp-fiscal-brasil" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
              </li>
              <li>
                <a href="/mcp-juridico-brasil/">MCP Jurídico Brasil</a> - an open-source MCP server for legal-process lookups via CNJ DataJud, published on <a href="https://github.com/DeHor-Labs/mcp-juridico-brasil" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub</a>.
              </li>
            </ul>
            <h2>How to follow</h2>
            <p>
              Readers can subscribe by email per project from the home page, or use the global <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> and each project's own feed. Machine-readable summaries are available at <a href="/index.md">/index.md</a> and <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
